# bootstrap-pointer.conf — box-level override for lean bootstrap stamping.
#
# Install to $OC_CONFIG/bootstrap-pointer.conf (Mac: ~/.openclaw/, VPS:
# /data/.openclaw/). One word, nothing else:
#
#   pointer   DEFAULT. Managed blocks are stamped into AGENTS.md / TOOLS.md /
#             MEMORY.md as a compact pointer (heading + one-line summary +
#             the trigger phrases and hard gates that must bind inline + ONE
#             absolute path), and the VERBATIM full text is written to
#             <master-files>/bootstrap-references/<FILE>.
#
#   full      Managed blocks keep their full text inline, the way the roll
#             behaved before. Nothing else about the roll changes.
#
# Resolution order (first match wins):
#   1. $OPENCLAW_BOOTSTRAP_POINTER_MODE
#   2. this file
#   3. agents.defaults.bootstrapPointerMode in openclaw.json
#   4. pointer
#
# An unrecognised value is treated as "pointer" and warns — honouring a typo as
# "full" would silently re-bloat the box, which is the failure this is here to
# prevent.
#
# Related: OPENCLAW_BOOTSTRAP_POINTER_MIN_CHARS (default 800) leaves blocks
# smaller than that inline, since pointerizing them saves nothing.
pointer
